      "status": "verified_correspondence",
      "status_text": "An estimator with nondecreasing additive error a and a positive gap computed in paid polynomial time in N+k gives one actual sparse 3-SAT algorithm whenever 2a(S(N,k))<k eventually. The same fixed construction constants support both size bounds and all four deterministic/randomized combinations. The algorithm has charged time polynomial in S; it is deterministic when both choices are deterministic, and bounded-error randomized otherwise. Accuracy on dyadic square tables suffices. The approved DinurReduction and BOTReduction (booleanOccurrence D) source interfaces remain explicit; their published-source fidelity remains the inherited author-owned qualification. No ETH assumption is used.",
